      "commandReview": [
        "README Python 3.13 pip requirements paths exist. Desktop default.pyw dispatches the WebView2-backed desktop entry; --legacy selects retained Tk UI. web_app.py is the private-loopback browser entry and requires the built frontend/dist. These Windows development commands are not Android APK installation commands.",
        "npm ci --prefix frontend resolves the committed package lock. npm run build --prefix frontend maps to vite build in frontend/package.json; the postinstall security-backport script is explicitly present. Vite 8.3.5 declares Node ^20.19.0 || >=22.12.0, so the documented Node 22 line requires a supported 22.12+ minor. No npm install, postinstall or product command was executed by this reviewer.",
        "English and Chinese README channel tables distinguish desktop 4.1.0, Windows web 4.2.0-web and the public Android 3.3.1 Beta. Android prerelease status, signed package/versionCode 5, SDK24/target36 and ARM64+x86_64 match source metadata and the public SDK/download receipts. Historical Windows channels were source-reviewed, not newly installed or promoted.",
        "The active Android guide requires checksum/certificate verification, explicit HTTP compatibility consent and a verified external schema-1 note backup before uninstall. It does not promise full-state/credential migration. Session exports exclude credentials; a profile review neither tests nor stores account data."
      ],
